1
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to my place!

2
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,948
Look at the blue sky,

4
00:00:33,998 --> 00:00:36,140
and the white clouds.

5
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:42,720
Somehow it'll all work out eventually.

6
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

7
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

8
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,940
Look, even the blazing sunset sky.

9
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow it'll all work out eventually.

10
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,560
You get it, right?

11
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,500
I get it, I get it.

12
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you get it, quietly follow me.

13
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:44,360
Miserable, terrible, birthday again.

14
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:55,900
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?

15
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,780
I'm trying to figure
out how to spend tomorrow.

16
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:03,760
That's right, tomorrow is March 3rd,
Ryo-san's birthday.

17
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:06,640
Every year on my birthday,
I get nothing but bad luck.

18
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,400
Going to work was bad,
staying home was bad too.

19
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,140
Kaper-ga -

20
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,020
No good, I'm sure to lose badly.

21
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:17,900
Then how about pachinko?

22
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,420
Pachinko?

23
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:25,100
Losing would be bad enough, but the ceiling might
collapse and pachinko balls might rain down on me.

24
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:28,620
How about going to a manga café
and reading comics to pass the time?

25
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,240
A manga café

26
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,920
I have a feeling a fire
would break out there.

27
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,420
Aren't you worrying a little too much?

28
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:36,280
That's not true.

29
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:39,120
I've been through terrible things before,
you know!

30
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:44,880
But bad things happening to you isn't really limited to your birthday, is it?
It just feels that way.

31
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:50,440
Ryo-san always seems to be getting into terrible trouble,
doesn't he?

32
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:54,460
Yeah, he's always causing some kind of trouble,
year-round.

33
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:55,240
I see.

34
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:58,160
Senpai, you're under self-suggestion.

35
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,720
Self-suggestion?

36
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:04,940
If you believe today is a bad day,
only the bad things stick in your memory,

37
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:08,760
but if you think it's a good day,
the good things are what you remember.

38
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,820
Depending on your mindset,
a day can be good or bad.

39
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:16,880
Ryo-chan is convinced that bad
things always happen on his birthday,

40
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:20,040
so it feels like nothing
but bad things happen to him.

41
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,720
But in reality,

42
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:26,160
I know! Let's throw Ryo-chan
a birthday party tomorrow!

43
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,320
What, really?

44
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:33,880
Okay, Ryo-chan, after your shift I'll
really put my heart into cooking you a meal.

45
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,940
I'll get a present ready too.

46
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:37,400
Then I'll also

47
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:44,200
let's invite Honda-san, Volvo-san,
and Sakonji-san too and make it a fun party.

48
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:50,060
But what if some incident happens
and the party gets cancelled?

49
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:53,020
Thinking like that isn't good.

50
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:54,100
That's right.

51
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,720
Tomorrow is going to be a good day.

52
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,160
If you believe that, it will be a good day.

53
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,040
Got it.

54
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:12,040
Ugh, my birthday has come
around again this year.

55
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:15,680
A message?

56
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:20,140
I think today will be
a lucky day for Ryo-chan.

57
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,580
Just believe that.

58
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,200
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

59
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,060
What a beautiful day it is.

60
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,320
Today looks like it's
going to be a good day.

61
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:35,240
Sorry. Right off the bat, this?

62
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,560
You bastard.

63
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:41,054
I think today will be
a lucky day for Ryo-chan.

64
00:04:41,104 --> 00:04:42,140
Just believe that.

65
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,220
That's right. I'm lucky today.

66
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:46,777
Yeah. No, wait,

67
00:04:46,827 --> 00:04:50,260
Thanks to that, I saved myself
the trouble of washing my face.

68
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:53,200
That was the water I wrung
out a dishrag in, though.

69
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:58,540
Well, I'll grab a bite to eat and head out.

70
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:01,260
My onigiri...

71
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:04,860
My onigiri!

72
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:06,440
Hey, give it back!

73
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:08,500
Wait!

74
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,940
Damn it, what a disaster!

75
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,520
My breakfast was

76
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,320
today is going to be

77
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,340
a lucky day for you, Ryo-chan, I think.

78
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,800
Just believe it.

79
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:23,000
Yeah, today I'm lucky.

80
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,000
That's right.

81
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,220
Reiko's supposed to have prepared
a mountain of great food today.

82
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:29,120
I should've skipped a meal.

83
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,300
If I'd eaten that onigiri,

84
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,700
I'd have been unable to eat the good food.

85
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,720
Lucky, lucky!

86
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:46,040
The sandals I've worn for years

87
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:49,200
maybe all my bad luck until now

88
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,800
was because of these sandals.

89
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,720
Yeah, yeah, that must be it.

90
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,360
Since we're having a party tonight,

91
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,340
it'd be good to change things up a bit.

92
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:01,940
Good thing they broke.

93
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,740
The brakes aren't working!

94
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,660
It's a dead end!

95
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,520
Yaaaah! Yaaaah!

96
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:24,220
Lucky I landed somewhere soft.

97
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,900
Water! Water! Water! Water!

98
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:30,820
Whoa!

99
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:32,660
Ugh...

100
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,300
Good thing there's a river nearby.

101
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,380
Senpai's late, isn't he?

102
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:47,660
Maybe he's skipping out.

103
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:49,660
I'm right here, you know!

104
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:53,920
Ryo-chan.

105
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,800
What happened, Senpai?

106
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:59,320
I just went all the way to Tokyo Bay.

107
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,400
What for?

108
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:02,180
All sorts of things happened.

109
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:05,580
Tonight's party is all about you,
Ryo-chan, so...

110
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:07,600
Don't go wandering off on your own, okay?

111
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,460
I know that.

112
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:14,820
I had the world's three great delicacies sent in for you,
senpai: truffles, foie gras, and caviar.

113
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,780
Please eat to your heart's content.

114
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,000
Really?

115
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,400
Yes, and we've also got fine
liquors from all over the world.

116
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,600
Lucky!

117
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:28,540
Now that's something to look forward to.

118
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:33,620
Senpai, why don't you go soak
at the public bath or something?

119
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,213
That's right. Tonight's a party, so

120
00:07:36,263 --> 00:07:38,320
go and freshen up, body and soul.

121
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,040
Yeah, you're right. I think I will.

122
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,680
See you later!

123
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,100
W-what! So many crows!

124
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,360
What? What's going on?

125
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:07,680
Ryo-chan

126
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,720
Hurry up and let go already!

127
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,360
Ryo-chan

128
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,840
Where are you going?

129
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:13,760
How would I know!

130
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,720
All three of us together,

131
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,340
triple joy!

132
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:18,280
OK.

133
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:21,620
Alright, next, set up the trampoline!

134
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,000
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

135
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,300
Come on, let go, let go!

136
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,400
Stop it!

137
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,000
Stop it!

138
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:47,420
Senpai, what about the bathhouse?

139
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,900
If I step outside from here now,

140
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,300
I've got a feeling I
won't be able to come back.

141
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,280
I see.

142
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,460
Ryo-san,

143
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:57,580
it's time for patrol, though.

144
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,980
You two go ahead.
I'll stay behind and mind the box.

145
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,660
Don't worry, Ryo-chan.

146
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:08,640
If the birthday party goes off without a hitch,
all your bad luck will be blown away in an instant.

147
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,620
I sure hope so.

148
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:12,500
Well, I'm off.

149
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:15,060
Wait! I have some business
at the station, too.

150
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:17,660
Ryo-chan, mind the fort while we're gone.

151
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:20,280
Yeah, I'm not setting foot outside today.

152
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:20,840
Well, then.

153
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:26,500
Man, I'm bored.
Guess I'll build a model kit.

154
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,000
Here we go.

155
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,820
This leaves the desk pretty cramped.

156
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,960
Hello?

157
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:43,680
Senpai, I found a really
interesting shop while on patrol.

158
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,000
An interesting shop.

159
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,460
It's an old toy shop, and I think there
might be some rare stuff you'd like.

160
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,720
What, really?

161
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,560
Fine, I'm coming right now.

162
00:09:56,380 --> 00:10:01,120
If I go outside right now, I've got a
feeling I'll never be able to come back here.

163
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,040
Senpai, what's wrong?

164
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:05,740
Anyway, there's nothing good there.

165
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,100
Going there is just a waste of time.

166
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,340
I said I'm not going,
and that means I'm not going!

167
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:10,100
But, Senpai...

168
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:14,280
So that these calls don't come again,
I'll turn off the power.

169
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:20,040
Just in case I accidentally step outside,
I'd better put handcuffs on myself.

170
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:23,040
But if I put them on,
I can't build my model kit.

171
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,380
There, that's better.

172
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:31,700
Somehow, all my fatigue has suddenly hit me.

173
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:34,100
With everything that's happened since this morning,
I guess.

174
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:41,520
Excuse me.

175
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,240
We've come to pick up the desk.

176
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,240
Hello?

177
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:48,580
Don't.

178
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,160
He's really bad when he first wakes up.

179
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:53,360
If you force him awake,
things will get really bad.

180
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:54,960
Is that so?

181
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,480
But which desk should we take?

182
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,960
It's probably this one.

183
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,700
Because there's nothing on top of it.

184
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:02,340
Let's load it onto the truck.

185
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:02,860
Right.

186
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,400
One, two, three!

187
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:35,600
Going to the bathroom made
me feel so much better.

188
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:37,660
All right, then let's go.

189
00:11:48,400 --> 00:12:11,060
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow
ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow

190
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:11,560
I'm back.

191
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,260
The desk is gone.

192
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:16,760
Now that I think about it, the old desk...

193
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,020
was supposed to be picked
up by the movers, but...

194
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:21,280
it wasn't even this desk.

195
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:22,720
Where's Ryo-san?

196
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:24,200
Ryo-san!

197
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:26,000
Where could he have gone?

198
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,400
He said he wouldn't leave
this spot for a single step.

199
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,780
I have a bad feeling about this.

200
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,520
Damn it, why are the handcuffs that
were supposed to be attached to the desk

201
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,800
over here?

202
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:43,900
I'm stuck! That's right, the key...
I locked it with the key.

203
00:12:56,300 --> 00:13:00,080
Damn, they got on the expressway!
Where do they think they're going?

204
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,220
Ryo-sama isn't here?

205
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:06,440
When we came back, he was already...

206
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:08,860
Maybe he went off to the horse races or pachinko,
don't you think?

207
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:12,380
But he was really looking
forward to today's party.

208
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:15,560
Besides, he said he didn't
want to leave the police box.

209
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,500
But it seems his phone is turned off.

210
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:22,120
For now, let's go ahead and get
the party preparations underway.

211
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:22,680
Yes.

212
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,320
Let's go look for Senpai.

213
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,940
Got it, I'll leave it to you.

214
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:29,840
Then I'll try calling my contacts too.

215
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,340
No way, is this snow?

216
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:38,880
Damn it, it's even snowing now!

217
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,840
Damn it,
the weather forecast was completely wrong.

218
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,000
It's turned into a blizzard.

219
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:48,140
Going this fast in this
cold only makes it colder.

220
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:50,540
The wind's coming off the river,
but it's still better.

221
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:52,640
If it's unauthorized, I'll report you.

222
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,240
What's wrong?

223
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:57,360
There was a person clinging
to the back of that truck!

224
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,560
No way, it was a painting, right?

225
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,140
That's the kind of thing
often painted on trucks.

226
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,700
Right. Yeah, that makes sense.

227
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,900
Still, it was a really realistic painting.

228
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,160
Man, my senses are going numb.

229
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,780
Whoa, that was close.

230
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:25,180
Oh right, I've got this.

231
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:29,080
I'll use my cell phone to
have Nakagawa come rescue me.

232
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:31,760
Yes?

233
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:35,780
Senpai, what happened?
You suddenly disappeared.

234
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,800
I don't understand it myself.

235
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:41,140
I fell asleep at the police box,
and before I knew it, I was outside.

236
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,920
So where are you now?

237
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,540
Aomori.

238
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:49,440
Looks like I'm heading for Hokkaido.

239
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:55,360
Damn, we're out of the prefecture?

240
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,300
No way.

241
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:04,280
Did you get in touch with Ryo-sama?

242
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:06,940
It cut off right away.

243
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,980
Did you find out where he is?

244
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,300
No, only that he's to the north.

245
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,240
Maybe he isn't around here?

246
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,660
I'll expand the search area.

247
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,540
We've finally made it
all the way to Hokkaido.

248
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:40,240
What is this road? It's not paved!

249
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:43,140
Ow ow

250
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,360
Damn, we took the wrong road.

251
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:49,300
We have to get onto the road
on the other side of that river.

252
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,140
What? Don't worry.

253
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:55,220
A river that shallow,
we can probably wade across.

254
00:15:56,020 --> 00:16:00,320
Hey, we're headed for Tomoe!

255
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:03,320
Aaaaaaah!

256
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,200
Aaaaaaah!

257
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,160
Aaaaaaah!

258
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:06,240
Me!

259
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,260
Me!

260
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:12,440
Mm.

261
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:12,500
Mm.

262
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:12,860
Mm.

263
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:13,440
Mm.

264
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,500
It's stopped moving.

265
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,740
Seems like we got caught on something.

266
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,120
Seems like we got caught on something.

267
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:26,220
Seems like we got caught on something.

268
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:27,960
Seems like we got caught on something.

269
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,620
Seems like we got caught on something.

270
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:31,200
Seems like we got caught on something.

271
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:33,100
Seems like we got caught on something.

272
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:42,040
Seems like we got caught on something.

273
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,640
Guess I forgot.

274
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,280
Turned out to be pretty deep.

275
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,920
I almost stalled out.

276
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,740
I thought I was going to die.

277
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,100
Somehow I got the handcuffs off.

278
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:06,040
Alright, now I can get back to Kameari.

279
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:10,180
Why at a time like this?

280
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:19,700
Whoa! Stop this! I'm going back to Kameari!

281
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:23,420
The world's three great delicacies
and finest liquors are waiting for me!

282
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:27,460
W-what's that?

283
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:35,700
Why is there a bear?!
Aren't they still in hibernation season?!

284
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:40,660
Whoa!

285
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,860
Stay back!

286
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:54,460
Hey, stop it, cut it out!

287
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:58,660
I'm not tasty at all, you know!

288
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:03,560
Bears eat this stuff too

289
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:08,400
Take that! I'm not going down that easy!

290
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:11,020
No matter what, I'm going back to Kameari

291
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:14,460
to enjoy the three great delicacies as
snacks and drink the world's finest sake!

292
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:22,700
W-what the...!?

293
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:28,700
Hey, let go!
What do you think you're doing to me?!

294
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,240
Take this!

295
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:37,600
Come on, I'm going back to Kameari
to drink the world's finest sake!

296
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:38,600
Yes, yes!

297
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:41,280
Nailed it!

298
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,880
The third PET bottle rocket competition
is finally reaching its climax.

299
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:06,020
Now, the main event of the day:
the Rocket Life Fireworks!

300
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:11,280
Just how far will it fly?

301
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,240
The countdown has begun.

302
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:14,220
8

303
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,180
7

304
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:16,420
6

305
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:17,520
5

306
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:18,620
4

307
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:19,880
3

308
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:20,380
2

309
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:42,760


310
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,660
Damn, it's cold!

311
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:58,860
Dammit, I've ended up in the Arctic again,
just like last year.

312
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:01,460
March 3rd is always the worst.

313
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:04,100
No, the day isn't over yet.

314
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:08,020
If I make it to the party,
all this hardship will be a funny story.

315
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,120
What?

316
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:13,540
It's a bear!

317
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,460
So you want to fight me

318
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:22,700
I'm not going to go down
without a fight, either.

319
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:25,300
No matter what, I'm going back to Kameari.

320
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:37,060
The world's three great delicacies, world-famous specialties,
and presents from everyone are waiting for me, you know!

321
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:46,500
This plane is receiving every kind of surveillance
footage from around the world in real time.

322
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:49,280
We're bound to find Senpai.

323
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:53,360
Chief, we've spotted
someone who looks like him.

324
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:54,520
Really?

325
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,780
Yes, take a look.

326
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:56,900
Enlarge it.

327
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:57,400
Yes.

328
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:00,660
Senpai!

329
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:01,460
Ryotsu!

330
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,980
Damn it, there are still this many?

331
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:14,340
No good, we can't possibly settle this.

332
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:16,540
Just as I thought, March 3rd is...

333
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:17,980
What?

334
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,100
Senpai!

335
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:21,620
Nakagawa.

336
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:22,940
Senpai!

337
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:24,400
Hang on, Ryotsu!

338
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:38,000
Whoa, are you okay, senpai? Well, somehow...

339
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,240
Detection complete.

340
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:52,300
Thank goodness you're safe! The party
preparations are all set. March 3rd isn't over yet!

341
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,860
Let's make it the best day ever.

342
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:00,220
This is...

343
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,300
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

344
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,360
Senpai, this is my gift to you.

345
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:13,200
A 50-inch plasma TV!

346
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,920
And now, game software too.

347
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:19,460
Isn't this the limited-edition Sensha
Yarō that came out three years ago?

348
00:22:19,460 --> 00:22:20,840
How did you manage to get this?

349
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,840
I bought it at that toy shop,
like we planned.

350
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:25,920
Here's something from me.

351
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,480
It's a token of my love.

352
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:31,360
Thank you, everyone.
It's the best day of my life!

353
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:34,280
Come on, Ryo-chan,
blow out the candles on the cake.

354
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:37,680
Reiko's homemade cake? Nice!

355
00:22:42,180 --> 00:22:44,020
Hello? Colonel.

356
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:46,340
Yes, Ryotsu has been found safe and sound.

357
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:47,960
Yes, understood.

358
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:50,600
What, is it from Colonel Bakuryu?

359
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:54,260
They've been helping
with the search for you.

360
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:55,500
How did it go?

361
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,440
They're flying over this area now.

362
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:00,420
They say they're dropping off presents.

363
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,580
Dropping?

364
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:03,980
That's the sound of a helicopter.

365
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,880
It looks like a tank model, doesn't it?

366
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,440
That's great, senpai.

367
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:17,020
I love tanks and stuff.

368
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:21,460
But somehow it seems way too big.

369
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:22,760
Yeah.

370
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:26,940
No! That's the real thing!

371
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:34,180
There's a present inside the barrel!

372
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:35,320
Look out! It's dangerous!

373
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:38,900
My plasma TV, my games, my party!

374
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:49,680
March 3rd has just ended.

375
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:53,340
Yeah, this year too,
it was the worst day, as always.

376
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:56,289
Damn it!

377
00:23:56,339 --> 00:23:59,720
That's why I hate March 3rd!

378
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:24,380
To the guy who has a stupid
showdown on the loops,

379
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:27,380
I probably don't want to become him.

380
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:31,980
If I'm dawdling at the street corner,

381
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:34,320
the moon has run away.

382
00:24:35,300 --> 00:24:38,200
Because now isn't everything.

383
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:42,580
Don't get so worked up about it.

384
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:46,280
Even if you lie and cheat a little,

385
00:24:47,140 --> 00:24:50,440
sometimes you're helping someone.

386
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,460
Baby, do you know me?

387
00:24:52,460 --> 00:24:56,900
Facing tomorrow with a nice, spirited heart.

388
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:01,820
Don't lose heart, just do what needs doing.

389
00:25:01,820 --> 00:25:04,240
A cute spirit.

390
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:07,760
What's hard to understand is

391
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:11,480
just because I want to look that way.

392
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:17,200
Better than all show
and no substance, right?

393
00:25:30,300 --> 00:25:33,800
When we were kids,
we were inspired by adventure movies.

394
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:37,260
We decided to float down the
Sumida River on a homemade raft.

395
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:40,500
An adventure journey from
Senju Ohashi to Tsukudajima.

396
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:43,680
But it doesn't go as smoothly as in the movies,
does it?

397
00:25:44,220 --> 00:25:46,220
Next time: Kankichi's adventure!

398
00:25:55,260 --> 00:25:59,220
Everyone, come to our town!

399
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:00,780
Thank you.

